      "id": "u_37c8756c90beeaaa09973cae_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "For performance and layout reasons, the size of widgets in Trilium is independent from its children. At CSS level, this means that the widget container has __TRILIUM_PH_0__ applied to it.",
      "sourceHash": "37c8756c90beeaaa09973cae35e380c1e6fe3d7d42b3dd2722e78e32e8596bf0",
      "context": "Troubleshooting > Why is my widget clipped by other UI elements",
      "contextHash": "629e21340bacab1aa6dac6c6db72f15881dfcb73136c120f1b344aec3cf8ccd8",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_13975086a7294b0dc003fa5b_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "This works well if the widget has a fixed size (or based on its parent container), however to make a widget resize to fit its content, apply the following change:",
      "sourceHash": "13975086a7294b0dc003fa5ba57cf285f09cf6e4e1096d27a1a4286219b0817e",
      "context": "Troubleshooting > Why is my widget clipped by other UI elements",
      "contextHash": "629e21340bacab1aa6dac6c6db72f15881dfcb73136c120f1b344aec3cf8ccd8",
      "status": "pending",
      "active": true
    },
    {
      "id": "u_492eda0b47b86ae29de6ba24_0",
      "kind": "p",
      "source": "Alternatively apply __TRILIUM_PH_0__ to its CSS.",
      "sourceHash": "492eda0b47b86ae29de6ba2495fe9204d47e375ddd23e065c7d88ed0dcd0c2d2",
      "context": "Troubleshooting > Why is my widget clipped by other UI elements",
